  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 255 PM CDT Mon Jun 29 2026\n\nFor the long term, we will start with extensive upper level \nridging over the southeastern U. S., and an upper level trough \nover the western half of the CONUS, leaving west-central Texas \nstill under southwest flow aloft. This pattern will keep us hot, \nwith somewhat windy conditions through Wednesday. As we move \ntowards this weekend, upper level ridging will gradually build \nover northern Mexico, merging with the southeastern CONUS ridge \nover our region. This will keep our temperatures hot. Ridging over\nthe top as opposed to southwesterly flow will also result in \nlighter winds, especially from Friday into the weekend.",
